From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:22:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(models): export complete asset pairs and empty item
 fallbacks

Java rejects a select model with no cases. Emit minecraft:empty when no
geometry was converted and preserve selectors for actual alternatives.
Only export complete geometry/texture pairs and bind their particle sprite
so Java does not bake dangling texture references.

Server declarations can include unused variants whose images are omitted.
Retain their missing-asset reasons as converter metadata and report an
actively selected custom actor model. An omitted inactive variant does
not prevent joining. Native rendering performs its own active lookup.

Saved Geyser and CubeCraft pack audits contain no dangling sprite or
particle bindings. Semantic tests cover empty and populated item exports,
resolved and unresolved model pairs, and inactive versus active failures.
